            <description><![CDATA[<style>
:root { color-scheme: light dark; }
body { font-family: -apple-system, 'Helvetica Neue', sans-serif; font-size: 13px; color: #1a1a1a; margin: 12px; }
@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
  body { color: #e6e6e6; }
}
h2 { font-size: 15px; margin: 0 0 8px; } ul { margin: 4px 0 10px; padding-left: 20px; } li { margin-bottom: 3px; }
p { margin: 4px 0 10px; }
</style>
<h2>Asobi 0.2 (build 430)</h2>
<p><b>Open Recent, dependable double-clicks, and portable sessions.</b></p>
<ul>
<li><b>File → Open Recent</b> remembers your last ten sessions, folders, and clips — reopening a session restores its whole playlist, and reopening a folder re-scans everything in it.</li>
<li>Double-clicking a session now always opens it in the window in front of you — previously, with restored windows around, it could quietly load into a background window while the front one kept its old state.</li>
<li><b>Settings → Sessions → Save with relative media paths</b>: media stored alongside the session saves Nuke-style relative references, so the whole folder moves or remounts without breaking.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
